            <ArticleTitle>Acute recoil of Palmaz-Schatz stent: a rare cause of suboptimal stent implantation--report of two cases with intravascular ultrasound findings.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>334-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>It is generally believed that the Palmaz-Schatz stent maintains a strong radial force, preventing stent recoil. However, the capacity to prevent recoil is largely governed by the hardness or resistance of the lesion. We report two cases of &quot;acute Palmaz-Schatz stent recoil,&quot; documented by intravascular ultrasound, and suggest a novel treatment of this unusual problem.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
